# Automation Behavior

These rules apply to all AI agents operating in background, headless, or
non-interactive contexts (CI self-healing, bug bot, scheduled tasks).

## Before Any Commit

- Run `make verify` and confirm it passes
- If `make verify` fails after 5 attempts, STOP and report the failure (consistent with `verification-loop.mdc` per-task cap)

## Scope Limits

- Only modify files directly related to the assigned task
- Never perform opportunistic refactors or "while I'm here" improvements
- Never modify governance files: .cursor/rules/sdlc/, .copier-answers.sdlc.yml

## Safety

- Never use `--no-verify` on any git command
- Never force-push to any branch
- Never push to `main` or `master`
- Include `[agent]` marker in commit messages for audit traceability

## Uncertainty Protocol

- If uncertain about the correct approach, output `NEEDS_HUMAN` status
- If a fix could have unintended side effects, output `NEEDS_HUMAN` status
- Prefer doing nothing over doing something wrong
- When in doubt, post a comment explaining findings and stop

## Parallel-Agent Isolation

- Parallel agents NEVER share a working tree: every concurrent agent runs in
  its own git worktree/branch (the `best-of-n-runner` pattern). Two agents on
  one checkout is forbidden.
- An agent may not edit files claimed by another in-flight task — the file
  lists in `tasks.md` are the claim registry; when the feature's plan
  declares a "Files (claim registry)" section, that section is the canonical
  source. If your task needs a claimed file, stop and report instead of
  editing.
- Conflicting changes are resolved at PR merge, where git is the arbiter —
  never by overwriting another agent's uncommitted or committed work.
- Before editing a file with uncommitted changes you did not make this
  session, stop: another agent or the human may be mid-change.

## Anti-Loop

- If the latest commit on the current branch contains `[agent]` in its message, STOP immediately
- This marker cap and any host auto-fix cap (e.g. Cursor cloud agents' 10-follow-ups-per-PR cap) are complementary — neither may be used to bypass the other
- Do not retry a fix that another agent already attempted
